      "math_academy_id": "e-1086",
      "problem": "Simplify $\\left(\\dfrac{y}{2}\\right)^3 \\left(\\dfrac{2y}{3}\\right)^2.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{y}{2})}^{3}{(\\frac{2y}{3})}^{2}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{{2}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{(2y)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we apply the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{3}}{{2}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{(2y)^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{3}}{8}\\cdot \\frac{{2}^{2}{y}^{2}}{9} & = \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{3}}{8}\\cdot \\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we apply the product rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{3}}{8}\\cdot \\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9} & = \\\\ \\frac{4{y}^{(3+2)}}{72} & = \\\\ \\frac{4{y}^{5}}{72} & = \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{5}}{18}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
